{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSYYKXubcu15LYb1eYND","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a shipment that is in the CANCELLED state.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new `@PostMapping` method `confirm` that:\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as a path variable\n   - Looks up the shipment using `repository.findById(shipmentId)`\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if the shipment doesn't exist (404)\n   - If the shipment exists:\n     - If status is CREATED: update to CONFIRMED and save\n     - If status is CONFIRMED: do nothing (idempotent)\n     - If status is CANCELLED: throw `ConflictException` with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n   - Returns the (possibly updated) shipment in a ResponseEntity\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without changes\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 Conflict\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 Not Found\n\n**Alternative approaches considered and rejected:**\n- Creating a separate ConfirmShipmentService: This would add unnecessary complexity for a single operation. The logic is simple enough to live in the controller, following the existing pattern.\n- Using HTTP PATCH instead of POST: The ticket explicitly requests POST, and POST is appropriate for state transitions.\n- Adding a new exception type (InvalidStateException): Using existing ConflictException is consistent with how the API handles other conflicts. Creating a new exception type would duplicate the error handling infrastructure.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n**Case 1: Confirm CREATED shipment**\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-1/confirm` where S-1 exists in CREATED state\n- Flow: Controller calls `repository.findById(\"S-1\")` → returns Shipment with CREATED status → creates new Shipment with CONFIRMED status → calls `repository.save(confirmedShipment)` → returns 200 OK with updated shipment\n- Output: Shipment object in JSON with status=\"CONFIRMED\"\n\n**Case 2: Confirm CONFIRMED shipment (idempotent)**\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-2/confirm` where S-2 exists in CONFIRMED state\n- Flow: Controller calls `repository.findById(\"S-2\")` → returns Shipment with CONFIRMED status → detects status is already CONFIRMED → saves unchanged shipment → returns 200 OK with same shipment\n- Output: Shipment object in JSON with status=\"CONFIRMED\" (unchanged)\n\n**Case 3: Confirm CANCELLED shipment**\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-3/confirm` where S-3 exists in CANCELLED state\n- Flow: Controller calls `repository.findById(\"S-3\")` → returns Shipment with CANCELLED status → detects CANCELLED state → throws ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → returns 409 Conflict with error envelope\n- Output: Error response with code=\"SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\"\n\n**Case 4: Confirm non-existent shipment**\n- Input: `POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm` where S-missing doesn't exist\n- Flow: Controller calls `repository.findById(\"S-missing\")` → returns null → throws ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → returns 404 Not Found with error envelope\n- Output: Error response with code=\"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\"\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test confirming CREATED → CONFIRMED**: Create a shipment in CREATED status, POST to confirm endpoint, verify status is CONFIRMED in response and status is 200 OK\n2. **Test idempotent confirm**: Create a shipment, confirm it twice, verify both succeed and the second returns the same state\n3. **Test CANCELLED state rejection**: Directly save a CANCELLED shipment to repository, POST to confirm endpoint, verify 409 response with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n4. **Test non-existent shipment**: POST to confirm endpoint with non-existent shipment ID, verify 404 response with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1094,"cache_read_input_tokens":17490,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1094},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dead460-0b04-48a2-b143-4cb6d1dbdc20","uuid":"c097978d-f41b-4b26-af1b-d11ec63a3b9b","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:44:02.799Z","request_id":"req_011CfSYYK7rck2mh8XNqQEDw"}
